1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:02,725
Three documents.

2
00:00:02,805 --> 00:00:04,478
Each one looks anonymous.

3
00:00:04,558 --> 00:00:06,045
But put them side by side,

4
00:00:06,125 --> 00:00:09,112
and they point to just one person.

5
00:00:12,103 --> 00:00:13,358
This is Mosaic.

6
00:00:13,438 --> 00:00:15,274
It catches what you never realized you

7
00:00:15,354 --> 00:00:17,261
were revealing.

8
00:00:18,989 --> 00:00:21,870
Redaction tools hunt for names and emails.

9
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:23,994
Mosaic checks how your next draft combines

10
00:00:24,074 --> 00:00:26,609
with everything you’ve already published.

11
00:00:26,857 --> 00:00:29,656
Your private documents never leave your browser.

12
00:00:29,736 --> 00:00:32,396
The cloud only writes generic test packs,

13
00:00:32,476 --> 00:00:34,312
from a fixed list of categories,

14
00:00:34,392 --> 00:00:38,089
and only after you approve the exact request.

15
00:00:38,169 --> 00:00:39,343
Open a workspace,

16
00:00:39,423 --> 00:00:41,363
hit review, and Mosaic lights up the

17
00:00:41,443 --> 00:00:42,756
passages that matter,

18
00:00:42,836 --> 00:00:45,717
with evidence from every release side by side.

19
00:00:45,797 --> 00:00:48,155
Every result says where it ran.

20
00:00:48,235 --> 00:00:50,535
With no built-in model on this machine,

21
00:00:50,615 --> 00:00:54,658
the sample shows clearly labelled sample results.

22
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:57,074
The disclosure map shows exactly how the

23
00:00:57,154 --> 00:00:59,396
draft connects to earlier releases.

24
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:00,952
In this fictional sample,

25
00:01:01,032 --> 00:01:03,773
three small details narrow a hundred people

26
00:01:03,853 --> 00:01:05,853
down to one.

27
00:01:06,202 --> 00:01:09,559
Mosaic suggests safer wording that keeps your point.

28
00:01:09,639 --> 00:01:11,381
Apply it, review again,

29
00:01:11,461 --> 00:01:14,974
and that group grows from one to twenty-one.

30
00:01:15,054 --> 00:01:16,239
Need new tests?

31
00:01:16,319 --> 00:01:18,515
You see the exact request before anything

32
00:01:18,595 --> 00:01:19,781
leaves your device.

33
00:01:19,861 --> 00:01:20,976
Just categories.

34
00:01:21,056 --> 00:01:21,940
No text.

35
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:23,827
No names.

36
00:01:23,907 --> 00:01:25,046
While building Mosaic,

37
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:26,393
we found a real gap.

38
00:01:26,473 --> 00:01:28,680
In browsers without the built-in model,

39
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:32,616
the SDK’s on-device-only mode quietly sends requests

40
00:01:32,696 --> 00:01:33,591
to the cloud.

41
00:01:33,671 --> 00:01:35,646
Mosaic’s guard blocks that.

42
00:01:35,726 --> 00:01:38,632
Zero private requests got through.

43
00:01:39,644 --> 00:01:41,642
Got a scan or a photo?

44
00:01:41,722 --> 00:01:43,558
Mosaic reads it with OCR,

45
00:01:43,638 --> 00:01:44,696
right on your device,

46
00:01:44,776 --> 00:01:48,239
and flags any words it isn’t sure about.

47
00:01:48,497 --> 00:01:50,205
Approve the release on your device,

48
00:01:50,285 --> 00:01:51,656
export a clean copy,

49
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:53,469
and you’re done.

50
00:01:53,907 --> 00:01:55,185
And it feels right at home on

51
00:01:55,265 --> 00:01:56,836
your phone.

52
00:01:57,841 --> 00:01:59,119
It’s measured, too.

53
00:01:59,199 --> 00:02:01,105
On our open synthetic benchmark,

54
00:02:01,185 --> 00:02:03,787
the rules baseline alone scores one hundred

55
00:02:03,867 --> 00:02:06,898
percent precision and forty-four percent recall.

56
00:02:06,978 --> 00:02:09,919
On-device model runs are next.

57
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:11,818
Mosaic.

58
00:02:11,898 --> 00:02:14,024
Protect the information you never realized you

59
00:02:14,104 --> 00:02:14,744
were revealing.

